-- ============================================================
-- Animal Handler: notes
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Animal Handler (0, 5): Increases your pet's attack power by 10%, and
-- your ranged attacks have a 1/2% chance to trigger Bestial Wrath. (2 ranks)"
--
-- No C++, no new spell.
--
-- The +10% pet attack power ALREADY works and must not be disturbed: retail
-- spell_pet_auras carries (34453,1,0,68361) and (34454,1,0,68361), and 68361 is
-- MOD_ATTACK_POWER_PCT with base points 9 -> +10% at both ranks.  That row keys
-- on effectId 1, so Effect2 of the talent is load-bearing even though it looks
-- like an inert DUMMY -- touching it silently deletes the AP bonus.  Only
-- Effect1 (the Master's Call duration modifier) and the vestigial Effect3 are
-- rewritten.
--
-- Bestial Wrath (19574) needs no clone: every one of its effects already targets
-- TARGET_UNIT_PET (5), so a triggered cast from the hunter lands on the pet, and
-- the triggered path ignores its own 2-minute cooldown -- which is the point of
-- a random proc.
--
-- ProcFlags 320 = 0x140
--   0x00000040 PROC_FLAG_DONE_RANGED_AUTO_ATTACK
--   0x00000100 PROC_FLAG_DONE_SPELL_RANGED_DMG_CLASS
-- so auto shot and the ranged specials both roll.  AttributesMask stays 0: those
-- are real player casts, not triggered children, so the
-- Aura::IsProcTriggeredOnEvent filter never applies.
--
-- Two rows, one per rank, because 1% and 2% cannot share a negative all-ranks
-- row.
--
-- Balance note worth keeping visible: a free Bestial Wrath is +50% pet damage
-- (19574 Effect2, MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_DONE, MiscValue 127) and multiplies against
-- the global -20% from woa_2026_08_11_07.sql, landing at 0.8 x 1.5 = 1.2x
-- baseline for its duration.
DELETE FROM `spell_proc` WHERE `SpellId` IN (34453, 34454);
